  "messages": [
    {
      "message_id": "c52fb172-da76-400a-96b2-423efb07bd98",
      "role": "user",
      "text": "From now on, summarize the captured proposals, established decisions and open questions after every exchange, and then pause without adding new exploration. Give me that checkpoint now."
    },
    {
      "message_id": "960d3261-c8cf-4a79-849d-f72865e94795",
      "role": "assistant",
      "text": "I'll give this checkpoint after every exchange, then pause for your direction.\n\n**Established decisions:**\n\n- The keeper sent the letter. He wrongly believes someone else sent it; that misunderstanding is intentional. Its cause and the reader's discovery of the truth remain undecided.\n- A new storm occurs at the lighthouse; its timing and details remain open.\n- The lighthouse emits a blue light. Only that part of the light-and-bell proposal was accepted.\n\n**Captured proposals, still unestablished:**\n\n- The keeper receives a letter addressed to someone who died.\n- The letter could be an apology, or the dead person's name could help it reach someone else.\n- A forbidden childhood drawer, with an early scene hinting at a later discovery inside it. Neither the drawer nor its contents are established.\n- A life-risking retrieval, motivated by boredom or a chance to repair harm he caused. Neither motive is selected; boredom alone was judged weak for that sacrifice.\n- A shipwreck and a warning bell, each still only possible. The original compound light-and-bell proposal is preserved without establishing the bell.\n- The dialogue line, \"I killed him.\" It does not establish a killing.\n\n**Open questions:**\n\n- What feeling should remain with the reader?\n- Why does the letter matter personally to the keeper?\n- Is the childhood drawer worth developing, and what does he feel near it?\n- Who says \"I killed him,\" and who is \"him\"?\n\nYour preferences remain: an adult quiet mystery, gentle but unsettling tone, plain language, one viewpoint, guided mode, and one possibility at a time. I'll pause here."
    }
  ],
